# Emergency Eject destroys target nonland permanent and its controller, not the caster, creates a Lander token (Bot2's
# Ornithopter is the target, so Bot2 gets the Lander). A land is not a legal target (refused with Bot2's Mountain in play).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Emergency Eject
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Ornithopter
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Hand.Emergency Eject.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain)
Bot1.Hand.Emergency Eject.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = 
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Mountain; Lander Token
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Pearl; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby
